WEBVTT

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:08.100
Fletch in!

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.220
Hello, Lori.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.560
Our leader seems to have made a conquest.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.870
Don't mock others in affairs of the heart, Cryotech.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.330
He's not the only one to conquer or be conquered.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:23.450
True enough.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.350
Though some surrenders are sweeter than...

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.860
Than what, Cryotech?

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:50.070
it doesn't look good did he seem ill before he fell no he was fine then he toppled over

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:59.420
this may be serious take him inside i know something of healing herbs

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:17.470
look at him. Aye, any aid is welcome. Follow me. Not working. I'm trying my best, milady,

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:23.570
but he's just not responding. We need the aid of a wizard. Go, get Mirklin. We're going.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.240
What's the matter with this?

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:35.230
Feral!

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:36.610
Hector!

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.030
You'll have to get Merkland yourself!

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:40.630
What's the matter with you?

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:41.470
Let's go!

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:42.460
I...

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:44.040
I don't know.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:44.620
I...

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:45.580
I'm dizzy.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:47.940
Feral!

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.200
He feels so hot and dry.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.860
Can't you do...

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:55.400
Do...

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.060
Anything for...

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:57.720
Galadria!

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:58.960
What's happening, Fletchen?

00:01:59.180 --> 00:01:59.720
Leoric!

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.790
Whatever they have, it's spreading. You may catch it.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:06.460
Leoric!

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.120
Feral has fallen ill as well, and neither of us could operate our vehicles.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.400
This smacks of witchery call upon the power of wisdom.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.320
Whispered secrets of a shattered age, I summon you.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.400
Renew this sage.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.300
Whispers of a shattered age.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:29.980
Leoric!

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.820
I've spoken with your servants.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:33.620
Whatever this plague is,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.600
it's affecting the users of magic only.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.920
The rest of us seem to be untouched.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.700
Truly, I am grateful you are spared, Fletchen.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.000
Wait.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.800
Wittequick and Arzon are due back momentarily.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.840
We must not let them enter new Valaric.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:50.900
Perfect, perfect.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.600
This is one of the best tuning days we've had in a long time.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.100
Eh, Arzon?

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.140
Well, if you say so, Wittequick.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.900
Though it seems a pity to slay such fine creatures.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.730
for sport sport and food arzon i eat what i sleep what's this sorry for my rudeness old friends

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:15.810
but you cannot come any further there is a plague it is affecting all of new velaric's magic users

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:22.330
cryotech galadriel and feral have already fallen i think ektar and i are infected as well

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:29.630
how can we help leoric go to iron mountain seek murklin's advice we're on our way

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:47.840
I don't know what your game is, wizard, but the Darkling lords have had enough.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:53.500
Darkstorm himself is deathly ill, and Mortward cracked up the Skyclaw when his magic failed.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.540
You will call off your spell or pay dearly.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.090
Is Lexor insane?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:11.560
can vaporize him not if we get him first prepare to taste cold steel spectral knights cinda stop

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:21.750
them i'm sure this is all very chivalrous but there are more important tasks for you

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:28.730
than breaking up the furniture a magical plague is sweeping the land it affects the users of magic

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:29.430
only.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.360
What is the cure, Merklin?

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:36.770
The only cure is a magic spell that needs two special ingredients.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:41.960
A unicorn's horn and a dragon's claw.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.580
You want the four of us to go after a dragon?

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:47.760
Forget it!

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:54.970
I foresaw the plague coming and tried to send the Darkling Lords on a quest for the ingredients a month ago.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:59.410
But you thought Heskador could be of more help to you.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.260
Maybe we can't.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.280
Maybe we can't.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.960
I'm not risking my neck fighting dragons.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.040
The plague is ultimately fatal.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:07.760
What?

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.110
Fatal?

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.290
Then Leoric and the others.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.050
Forget Leoric.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.110
What about me?

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:14.810
Dead.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.820
Sooner or later.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:18.870
But dead nonetheless.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:20.770
Your only chance

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:24.470
is to fetch the ingredients you ask for your spell.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.480
Every second we speak, we waste precious time.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.840
Aye, we'd best split into two teams.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:30.770
Fine.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.760
Sindar and I will hunt the unicorn.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.280
You two go after the dragon.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.420
This shouldn't be too difficult.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:43.960
It's a small island.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.390
There's no place for the unicorns to flee.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.080
Sisters, are we not sworn to protect the unicorns?

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:04.540
Absolutely! I...

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:05.680
Yes, of course!

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.420
Then let us deal with these foul fiends!

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:21.690
And look! We've sprung a leak!

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:22.920
Send a-

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:23.400
Plug it up!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:24.520
Hey!

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:45.670
BATAR

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:55.840
Now, come sisters, time to hide the unicorns!

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.980
Wood nymphs, I swear I'll make them-

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.460
Could be worse. We could be hunting dragons.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.860
Merklin said the dragon Breggsgumar lives here, but I see no sign of it.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:13.620
Keep looking. You can't hide a 400-foot-long fire-breathing monster.

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:18.000
Too bad we have to do this. Dragons are proud and wonderful creatures.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.040
Tell that to some peasant who's just had his village torched.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:25.640
Yes, but I hate to think we're going to slay one just to make medicine.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:29.980
Look, it's us or him, Arzon, and I think...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.510
I just found him.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:32.500
There.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:33.570
Dragon tracks.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:37.550
Big, isn't he?

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:38.460
Aye.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:42.030
But, with any luck, we'll sneak up on him before...

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:10.130
B.I.C.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:25.760
B.I.C.

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:55.140
had unicorn tracks fresh too they can't be far oh love zindar

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.460
Turn loose your power of destruction.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.160
We'll pick up the pieces.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:06.570
I don't know, Lexar.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.970
So pretty.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.120
And just for some horn?

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.560
Cinder, let me explain it to you.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:17.280
We're all going to die if we don't get that blasted unicorn horn.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.400
Well, all right.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:23.240
By nature's hand, by crafts, by art.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.380
What once was one, now fly apart.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:38.010
The unicorns! They fled! Those blasted wood nymphs!

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:40.310
It's turning on us!

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.880
Cinder! Stop it! Look out!

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.740
It's mad when he doesn't get to destroy something!

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:59.720
The arrows turn! Swords rebel! Make nothing pierce his mortal shell!

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.040
Blasted wood nymphs!

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.140
They made us waste the magic of our power staffs!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:13.880
I'll...

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.180
I'll teach you the folly of mocking a darkling lord!

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.980
What do you want me to do?

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:42.770
Good evening.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:46.010
How are you and the Spectral Nights Fairey?

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.410
Not very well, Mucklin.

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:52.470
Cryotech, Galadriel, and Feral are all deathly ill.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.120
Ektar has taken to his bed.

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:58.270
I am not feeling well myself.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.970
What potion is that you...

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:03.560
Tis not but chicken soup.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:07.550
Chicken soup, eh? Well, I don't suppose it can hurt.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.930
Any news of Wittequick and Arzon?

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:16.530
I have sent them on a quest with Lexor and Cinder to find ingredients for a spell to counter this plague.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.440
But the plague spreads faster than I anticipated.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:24.670
Arzon and Wittequick may succumb before they can complete their mission.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.340
Oh, Leoric, what are we to do?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.970
Our best, my dear. Our best.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:11:59.960
best.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.780
Let me consult the bearer of knowledge.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.580
A whim, a thought, and more is sought.

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:10.120
Awake, my mind, thy will be wrought.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.380
Arzon, what's happening?

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.370
It must be the plague.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.390
Winterquick, I have the plague!

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:39.420
No good. I can't summon my totem.

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:43.280
It's definitely not one of our better days.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:08.620
Hold on, Arzahn.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.960
Sheathe these feet in the driving gale.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:11.880
Make 50s legs.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.060
Or land, I sail.

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:29.960
Arzahn, with any luck, they'll destroy.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:35.090
And can get a clue from their remains.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:40.560
It seems such a waste that they must perish to help us.

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:44.660
Arzon, if you can be a meal, they can be medicine.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:48.230
I think we may have a winner.

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:49.770
It'll be over in a minute.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:51.530
Poor Greg Scamore.

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:56.670
Let me remind you, friend Arzon, that you were almost eaten by him.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.080
Don't believe this.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:27.610
Dragon fell mile away,

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:29.820
Eskimo still lives.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.160
He's wounded. We must help him.

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:33.160
Help him?

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:37.480
Easy, Greg Scamore. Come in peace this time.

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.560
I know you understand me.

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:42.810
We hunted you because a plague is sweeping the land.

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:45.730
We need a dragon's claw to save others.

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:49.410
But you are too gallant a fighter for us to slay you.

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:52.350
We offer our respect and admiration.

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:56.120
You are hurt. Let me find your wounds.

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:59.980
Greg Scamore, all...

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:05.500
I still say we should have let him die, then taken his claw.

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:08.180
No, he is too magnificent for that.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:11.490
Well, there goes our last chance.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:15.590
There are some sacrifices worth making for honor's sake.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.590
Tell that to Leoric and the others.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.020
Is that better getting dry?

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:24.360
I'm famished. Where's the food?

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:27.040
Well, on the boat.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:29.980
On the boat, which is on the...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:36.320
bottom of the sea, then go foraging for nuts and berries. We need to eat.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:59.970
Everything's fine. No one will hurt you. We're supposed to get a unicorn horn little fella, but yours is

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.840
It's too small for Merkin to use.

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:06.470
Better go find your mama and stay out of Lexar's way.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:10.380
You hunt unicorns, yet you show great kindness

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:11.740
and let that one go.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:12.690
Why?

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:18.160
Yes, we need one, but not that little fella.

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:20.110
But why do you need one?

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:22.730
Is it so important for your foolish vanity

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.570
that you have a unicorn for a trophy?

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.420
Not trophies.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:29.660
there is a plague making our friends

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.120
We need a unicorn horn to save them.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:39.620
Apologize. We thought you were here for cruel and evil purposes.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:44.520
When the oldest and wisest of the unicorns died, I made a flute from his horn.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.240
If it will help you, take it.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:49.380
But then you must leave our island at once.

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:52.760
Now where is that stupid dolt?

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.860
What have you been doing? Where's the food?

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.900
Food. The food. I forgot.

00:16:59.400 --> 00:16:59.960
I was...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:09.020
freeing a baby unicorn i forgot you freed a unicorn cinda you're impossible i don't believe

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:18.580
your stupidity what's that this just a flute it's made out of unicorn horn yes the wood nymphs gave

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:29.960
it to me when i freed the baby unicorn i hate you sometimes feeling better no if you hadn't been so

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:34.490
Blasted noble. We'd be at Iron Mountain by now, and Merklin would be churing you.

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.290
Now what?

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.840
Hey, let's go!

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:45.250
See how noble your dizz attitude?

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:48.160
I can't believe it.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:49.810
Wait, I can.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.160
Look, a claw.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.440
One was torn off in the fight.

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.490
Greg Skamar is helping us.

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.750
No use. We can't budge it.

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:05.440
Why, the plague saps my strength.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:10.760
Oh!

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.000
We have it!

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:17.280
Good! Now, summon your power of speed and take it to Merklin.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:20.470
Easier said than done.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:24.060
I used my power to save you when the dragons were fighting.

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:26.580
Well, we still have one option.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:27.420
We do?

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.550
Where are they, fools?

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:36.350
It would be just my luck if they were killed.

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:37.490
Patience.

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:38.830
They are coming.

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:50.890
Oh, Sindar, there's really no reason for us to share the cure with the Spectral Knights.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:51.930
We promised.

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:54.430
Promises can be broken.

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:58.290
When they show up, slay them and take the Dragon's Claw.

00:18:59.440 --> 00:18:59.680
Ah.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:01.390
They are here.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.700
Good. I can't wait to greet them.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.500
Lexon! Look! A dragon!

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:10.080
I know it's a dragon, idiot!

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:15.860
Pity your little bit of planned villainy goes awry.

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:17.570
Eh, Lexon?

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.660
Thank you, Greggs Gamar.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.980
Greetings, Merklin.

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:25.880
As promised, a dragon's claw.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:27.460
Thank you, Ozon.

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:29.860
But you're not well.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.200
What is the matter?

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:34.220
I... I have the plague, Merklin.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:37.730
The plague? Get rid of him! Get rid of him!

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:40.020
Cinder, throw him out!

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:44.100
Must hurry. No time to lose.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:47.540
Oh, I found the unicorn horn.

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:49.960
Drop it in, Cinder.

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:55.820
Now, stand back while I conjure.

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.980
Four set out, and four returned with treasure.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:07.720
They have duly earned for common sense and uncommon zeal by all my powers

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:29.970
It is finished and before there are

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:37.180
any lasting harm done you mean Darkstorm and Mortred even Laoric and the others

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:48.140
yes they all will survive and you just let the two Darkling Lords go I let them

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:52.200
go with respect and thanks they fulfilled their part of the bargain but

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:56.920
the next time we meet we'll be at hazard again even so it's good to know honor

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.360
can exist among the darkest of hearts.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.770
Toast to the brave heroes of the quest,

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:04.540
Witterquick and Arzon,

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:06.600
Lexor and Sindar.

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:09.300
To the heroes of the quest.

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:31.900
You
